<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?><rdf:RDF xmlns:cc="http://creativecommons.org/ns#" xmlns:dct="http://purl.org/dc/terms/" xmlns:adms="http://www.w3.org/ns/adms#" xmlns:foaf="http://xmlns.com/foaf/0.1/" xmlns:odrl="http://www.w3.org/ns/odrl/2/" xmlns:owl="http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#" xmlns:dcat="http://www.w3.org/ns/dcat#" xmlns:lcon="http://www.w3.org/ns/locn#" xmlns:sioc="http://rdfs.org/sioc/ns#" xmlns:rdf="http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#" xmlns:rdfs="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#" xmlns:prov="http://www.w3.org/ns/prov#" xmlns:skos="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xmlns:schema="http://schema.org/" xmlns:v="http://www.w3.org/2006/vcard/ns#" xmlns:vann="http://purl.org/vocab/vann/" xmlns:voaf="http://purl.org/vocommons/voaf#" xmlns:wdrs="http://www.w3.org/2007/05/powder-s#" xmlns:xsd="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#" xmlns:spdx="http://spdx.org/rdf/terms#" xmlns:time="http://www.w3.org/2006/time#" xmlns:dcatap="http://data.europa.eu/r5r/" xmlns:stat="http://data.europa.eu/s1n/statdcat-ap/" xmlns:qb="http://purl.org/linked-data/cube#" ><dcat:Dataset rdf:about="http://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/web/products-datasets/-/cei_wm010"><dct:issued rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2017-11-27</dct:issued><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Zeitliche Frequenz</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Time frequency</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Fréquence (relative au temps)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Geopolitische Meldeeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Geopolitical entity (reporting)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Entité géopolitique (déclarante)</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Maßeinheit</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Unit of measure</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Unité de mesure</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="de">Abfallbewirtschaftungsmaßnahmen</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="en">Waste management operations</dcat:keyword><dcat:keyword  xml:lang="fr">Opérations de gestion des déchets</dcat:keyword><dct:type><skos:Concept  rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/dataset-type/STATISTICAL"/></dct:type><dct:title xml:lang="en">Recycling rate of all waste excluding major mineral waste</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="en">The indicator is calculated as recycled waste (RCV_R) divided by total waste treated excluding major mineral wastes (TRT), multiplied by 100. It is expressed in percent (%) as both terms are measured in the same unit, namely tonnes. Recycled waste is waste treated, which was sent to recovery operation other than energy recovery and backfilling (for simplification referred to as recycling). Waste data are adjusted for waste collected in one country and recycled in another country. The amount of recycled waste is adjusted as following: waste treated in domestic plants plus waste sent out of the country for recycling minus waste imported and treated in domestic recycling plants. Waste treated is based in Waste Statistics Regulation and the imports and exports of wastes are based on Foreign Trade Statistics and reported according to the &lt;a href=https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/ramon/nomenclatures/index.cfm?TargetUrl=LST_NOM_DTL&amp;StrNom=CN_2020&amp;StrLanguageCode=EN&amp;IntPcKey=&amp;StrLayoutCode=HIERARCHIC&gt;Combined Nomenclature&lt;/a&gt; (CN-codes). The indicator covers both hazardous (hz) and non-hazardous (nh) waste from all economic sectors and from households, including waste from waste treatment (secondary waste) but excluding most mineral waste. Major mineral waste is excluded in order to avoid situations where trends in ordinary waste generation can be drowned out by massive fluctuations in the generation of wastes in the mineral extraction and transformation sector. This also permits more meaningful comparison across countries, as mineral waste accounts for very substantial quantities in countries characterized by major mining and construction sectors.</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Taux de recyclage de tous les déchets sauf déchets minéraux principaux</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="fr">L’indicateur est calculé comme suit : déchets recyclés (RCV_R) divisé par le total des déchets traités à l’exception des déchets minéraux principaux (TRT) et multiplié par 100. Il est exprimé en pourcentage (%) puisque les deux composantes sont mesurées dans la même unité, i.e. des tonnes. Les déchets recyclés sont des déchets traités qui ont été envoyés pour récupération autre que la récupération d’énergie et le remblayage (nommé recyclage par simplification). Les données sur les déchets sont rajustées pour les déchets collectés dans un pays et recyclés dans un autre. La quantité de déchets recyclés est rajustée comme suit : (déchets traités dans des usines nationales) + (déchets exportés pour recyclage) – (déchets importés et traités dans des usines de recyclage nationales). Les déchets traités sont basés sur le Règlement des statistiques sur les déchets. Les importations et exportations de déchets se basent sur les statistiques du commerce extérieur et sont déclarés selon la Nomenclature Combinée (Codes NC) - &lt;a href=https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/ramon/nomenclatures/index.cfm?TargetUrl=LST_NOM_DTL&amp;StrNom=CN_2020&amp;StrLanguageCode=EN&amp;IntPcKey=&amp;StrLayoutCode=HIERARCHIC&gt;Combined Nomenclature&lt;/a&gt; (CN-codes). L’indicateur couvre à la fois les déchets dangereux et non-dangereux en provenance de tous les secteurs économiques et des ménages, incluant les déchets dérivés du traitement des déchets (déchets secondaires), mais excluant la plupart des déchets minéraux. Les déchets minéraux principaux sont exclus pour éviter que les fluctuations importantes dans la production de déchets de l‘extraction de minerai et le secteur de la transformation, n’influencent les tendances observées dans la production de déchets ordinaires. Cela permet également une comparaison plus significative entre les pays, étant donné que les déchets minéraux sont très conséquents dans les pays dont les secteurs de l’exploitation minière et de la construction sont très importants.</dct:description><dct:title xml:lang="de">Recyclingrate für alle Abfälle ohne dominante mineralische Abfälle</dct:title><dct:description xml:lang="de">Der Indikator wird berechnet indem recycelter Abfall (RCV_R) durch den gesamten behandelten Abfall ohne dominante mineralische Abfälle (TRT) geteilt und dann mit 100 multipliziert wird. Der Quotient ist in Prozent (%) ausgedrückt da beide Größen in derselben Einheit (Tonnen) gemessen werden. Recycelter Abfall ist behandelter Abfall, der zur Wiederverwertung geschickt wurde und nicht zur energetischen Verwertung und Verfüllung verwandt wurde (zur Vereinfachung wird er als recycelt bezeichnet). Die Abfalldaten sind bereinigt um Abfälle die in einem Land gesammelt und in einem anderen Land recycelt wurden. Die Menge des recycelten Abfalls ist wie folgt errechnet: in inländischen Anlagen behandelter Abfall plus zum Recycling aus dem Land ausgeführter Abfall minus eingeführter und in inländischen Anlagen behandelter Abfall. Behandelter Abfall wird im Sinne der Verordnung zur Abfallstatistik erfasst während Importe und Exporte im Sinne der Außenhandelsstatistik gemäß der “&lt;a href=https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/ramon/nomenclatures/index.cfm?TargetUrl=LST_NOM_DTL&amp;StrNom=CN_2020&amp;StrLanguageCode=EN&amp;IntPcKey=&amp;StrLayoutCode=HIERARCHIC&gt;Kombinierten Nomenklatur”&lt;/a&gt; (CN-Codes) verwandt werden. Der Indikator beinhaltet sowohl gefährliche (hz) als auch ungefährliche (nh) Abfälle aus allen Wirtschaftssektoren und von Haushalten, inklusive Abfall aus Abfallbehandlung (Abfall 2. Grades) aber ohne die meisten mineralischen Abfälle. Die wichtigsten mineralischen Abfälle sind ausgeschlossen um Situationen zu vermeiden, in denen Trends in der Erzeugung von normalen Abfällen durch massive Schwankungen des Abfallaufkommens bei der Gewinnung und Umwandlung von Bodenschätzen verwässert werden. Dies erlaubt auch eine bessere Vergleichbarkeit zwischen den Ländern, da in Ländern mit einem bedeutenden Bergbau- und Bausektor sehr große Mengen an mineralischen Abfällen anfallen.</dct:description><dct:identifier>cei_wm010</dct:identifier><foaf:page rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_wm010"/><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EUR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BEL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/BGR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CZE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DNK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/DEU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/EST"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/IRL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GRC"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ESP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FRA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HRV"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ITA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CYP"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LVA"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LTU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LUX"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/HUN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MLT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NLD"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/AUT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/POL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/PRT"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ROU"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SVK"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/FIN"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SWE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ISL"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/LIE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/NOR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/CHE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/GBR"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MNE"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/MKD"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/ALB"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/SRB"/></dct:spatial><dct:spatial><dct:Location rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/country/TUR"/></dct:spatial><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/FREQ" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Zeitliche Frequenz</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Time frequency</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Fréquence (relative au temps)</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/GEO" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Geopolitische Meldeeinheit</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Geopolitical entity (reporting)</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Entité géopolitique (déclarante)</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/UNIT" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Maßeinheit</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Unit of measure</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Unité de mesure</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:dimension> <qb:DimensionProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/WST_OPER" > <skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Abfallbewirtschaftungsmaßnahmen</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Waste management operations</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Opérations de gestion des déchets</skos:prefLabel> </qb:DimensionProperty> </stat:dimension><stat:attribute> <qb:AttributeProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/OBS_FLAG" /> </stat:attribute><stat:attribute> <qb:AttributeProperty rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/CONF_STATUS" /> </stat:attribute><stat:statUnitMeasure><skos:Concept rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/codelist/ESTAT/UNIT?code=PC"><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="de">Prozent</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="en">Percentage</skos:prefLabel><skos:prefLabel xml:lang="fr">Pourcentage</skos:prefLabel></skos:Concept></stat:statUnitMeasure><stat:numSeries rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer">28</stat:numSeries><dct:modified rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2024-11-28</dct:modified><dct:accrualPeriodicity><dct:Frequency rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/frequency/ANNUAL"/></dct:accrualPeriodicity><dct:temporal><dct:PeriodOfTime rdf:about="http://purl.org/dc/terms/PeriodOfTime/3169a64b-f3b3-4920-b709-b32c20b97678"><dcat:startDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2010-01-01</dcat:startDate><dcat:endDate rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#date">2022-12-31</dcat:endDate></dct:PeriodOfTime></dct:temporal><dct:accessRights><dct:RightsStatement rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/access-right/PUBLIC"/></dct:accessRights><dcat:landingPage><foaf:Document rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_wm010"><dct:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/documentation-type/WEBPAGE_RELATED"/><schema:url xml:lang="en">https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_wm010</schema:url><dct:title xml:lang="en">More information on Eurostat Website</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Plus d&apos;information sur le site web d&apos;Eurostat</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="de">Mehr Informationen auf der Eurostat Website</dct:title></foaf:Document></dcat:landingPage><foaf:page><foaf:Document rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/cache/metadata/en/cei_wm010_esmsip2.htm"><dct:title xml:lang="en">ESMS metadata (Euro-SDMX Metadata structure) HTML</dct:title><foaf:topic rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_wm010"/><schema:url xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/cache/metadata/en/cei_wm010_esmsip2.htm]]></schema:url><dct:format rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HTML"/><dcat:mediaType rdf:resource="http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/text/html"/><dct:type><skos:Concept rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/documentation-type/DOCUMENTATION_MAIN"/></dct:type></foaf:Document></foaf:page><foaf:page><foaf:Document rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/files?file=metadata/cei_wm010_esmsip2.sdmx.zip"><dct:title xml:lang="en">ESMS metadata (Euro-SDMX Metadata structure) SDMX</dct:title><foaf:topic rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/product/page/cei_wm010"/><schema:url xml:lang="en"><![CDATA[https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/files?file=metadata/cei_wm010_esmsip2.sdmx.zip]]></schema:url><dct:format rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/XML"/><dcat:mediaType rdf:resource="http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/application/xml"/><dct:type><skos:Concept rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/documentation-type/DOCUMENTATION_MAIN"/></dct:type></foaf:Document></foaf:page><dcat:distribution><dcat:Distribution rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/cei_wm010/default/table"><dct:title xml:lang="en">Table, graphs and map visualizations are also available.</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="fr">Des visualisations sous forme de tableau, graphique et carte géographique sont aussi disponibles.</dct:title><dct:title xml:lang="de">Tabellen, Grafiken und geografische Darstellungen sind ebenfalls verfügbar.</dct:title><dcat:accessURL rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/databrowser/view/cei_wm010/default/table"/><dct:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/distribution-type/VISUALIZATION"/><dct:license rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/licence/CC_BY_4_0"/><dct:rights rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/access-right/PUBLIC"/><dct:format rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/HTML"/><dcat:mediaType rdf:resource="http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/text/html"/></dcat:Distribution></dcat:distribution><dcat:distribution><dcat:Distribution rdf:about="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/data/cei_wm010?format=tsv&amp;compressed=true"><dct:title xml:lang="en">Download dataset in TSV format</dct:title><dct:type rdf:resource="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/distribution-type/DOWNLOADABLE_FILE"/><dcat:accessURL rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/data/cei_wm010?format=tsv&amp;compressed=true"/><dcat:downloadURL rdf:resource="https://ec.europa.eu/eurostat/api/dissemination/sdmx/2.1/data/cei_wm010?format=tsv&amp;compressed=true"/><dct:compressformat><dct:MediaTypeOrExtent rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/GZIP"/></dct:compressformat><dct:format><dct:MediaTypeOrExtent rdf:about="http://publications.europa.eu/resource/authority/file-type/TSV"/></dct:format><dcat:mediaType rdf:resource="http://www.iana.org/assignments/media-types/text/tab-separated-values"/><dct:license><dct:LicenseDocument rdf:about="http://